! Diamond: fcc, a = 6.74 Bohr (3.56665 Angstrom), two carbon atoms.
!
! The companion to tests/fixtures/h_sc.  Hydrogen has no core, so nothing in
! h_sc can test what happens when rhomt holds a frozen core; carbon's 1s
! carries two of its six electrons, so it does.  Two atoms of one species
! also exercise the atom-inner half of STATE.OUT's ias ordering, which one
! atom per cell cannot.
!
! The cell is verbatim the diamond cell in the sibling project's own
! Quantum ESPRESSO test input, so the two are comparable exactly rather
! than approximately.  Checked before running: the C-C distance is 2.91851
! Bohr = 1.54441 Angstrom with four neighbours, against a literature
! 1.5445 Angstrom.
!
! Everything else is left at Elk's defaults, exactly as in h_sc -- a typical
! run is the point -- with the two exceptions stated below.
!
! elk_init.in is this same input with tasks 9006 instead of 0 and 33.

tasks
  0
  33

! The species file is copied in beside elk.in so the fixture is portable.
sppath
  './'

! fcc primitive vectors, a/2 (0,1,1), (1,0,1), (1,1,0).
avec
  0.00  3.37  3.37
  3.37  0.00  3.37
  3.37  3.37  0.00

atoms
  1
  'C.in'
  2
  0.00  0.00  0.00    0.0  0.0  0.0
  0.25  0.25  0.25    0.0  0.0  0.0

! First exception to "Elk defaults": PBE, set explicitly rather than left at
! the default LSDA, so the fixture can be compared against a norm-conserving
! PBE pseudopotential calculation with no functional mismatch in the way.
! It also makes xcgrad = 1 in STATE.OUT's header, which h_sc cannot show.
xctype
  20

ngridk
  4  4  4

! Second exception, and here it is NOT a no-op as it was in h_sc: diamond's
! inversion centre is the bond midpoint at (1/8,1/8,1/8), so Elk's default
! (.true.) would move the origin there and leave STATE.OUT and GEOMETRY.OUT
! in a different frame from this atoms block.
tshift
  .false.

! plot3d box: the unit cell.  Origin, then the three lattice vectors as
! absolute corner vertices.  plotpt3d.f90 steps i/np3d without an endpoint,
! so with 16 points the second atom at 1/4 is exactly grid index (4,4,4).
plot3d
  0.00  0.00  0.00
  1.00  0.00  0.00
  0.00  1.00  0.00
  0.00  0.00  1.00
  16  16  16
